================================================================================
## Fix Load from GitHub doing nothing on Import
================================================================================

Context:
Registry → Import → Load from GitHub looked like a no-op: GitHubClient used
httpx `base_url` without a trailing slash and request paths with a leading
slash, so Git Data calls joined to `https://api.github.com/git/...` instead
of `/repos/{owner}/{repo}/git/...`. Test connection could still work because
`get_repo` used an absolute URL. The import modal also hid the spinner until
after the envelope download.

Changes:

1. src/back/core/github/GitHubClient.py
   Trailing slash on `base_url`; strip leading slashes so requests stay under
   the repo prefix. `get_repo` uses a relative GET.
2. tests/fixtures/github.py
   Reject calls that escape `/repos/acme/onto` so the join bug cannot regress
   in FakeGitHub.
3. tests/units/registry/test_github_client.py
   Assert tree/ref URLs keep the repo prefix.
4. src/front/static/registry/js/registry.js
   Show the preview spinner immediately, toast errors on GitHub read failure.
5. src/front/templates/partials/registry/_import_obx_modal.html
   Generic "Reading…" busy copy for file and GitHub.
6. tests/units/front/test_registry_obx_import_rename.py
   Contract: GitHub click shows busy and hits `/settings/github/obx`.

